{
  "$Comment": "What the Crafting and Enchanting trees' station stats pay at both Disenchanting Tables. Named by Extensions/DisenchantingProgression.json (and its greater child) and rolled once per ritual at the Payout beat. Each roll reads the MMO's station stats (Server/Entity/Stats/MMO_Station*.json in the MMO jar, each file saying what one point does) and nothing else: every stat is whole percent points read as a Chance, so 25 points is one ritual in four. A talent, gear carrying the stat or a buff all count the same, and with none of them every roll here reads 0 and pays nothing.\n\nTHE RETURN SHARE AND THE GUARDRAIL. Unmaking crafted gear must always lose materials: on the tightest pieces (two bolts in, one back) there is one unit of room, and Mmo_Disenchant_Salvage_Extras already pays up to three quarters of it. Every rpgstations:output_items a ritual grants sums before ONE resolution (the whole part lands, the fraction is the chance of one more), so a talent that paid a whole unit would stack on that three quarters and could hand back three for two. So every stat that adds more of the return (Crafting's main line MMO_StationYield_CRAFTING, Metal Reclaim's MMO_Station_Return and the everyday-find stat MMO_Station_Find) shares ONE slot here, read as a SHARE of one more, never a whole unit: their sum on a Ladder in whole points, each point a hundredth of a unit, held at 0.20 by the top floor, behind the same item level 15 gate. With the extras the most a ritual adds is 0.95 of a unit, under the one unit of room, so even a fully invested, lucky enchanter gets back less than went in. Raise the top floor only with the extras table lowered to match.\n\nThe rolls that repeat a find grant a Lootable reward naming the table to roll again with Trigger Cycle: the nested table is judged against this same ritual (the same piece, its level, quality and wear), so a second roll keeps every gate the first had. The conditional piece bonuses (the MMO_Station_Bonus_* stats) pay Essence of Life and a second void roll, never more of the return, for the guardrail above.\n\nEvery number here is balance data; retune by shipping a same-id file from a pack loading after this one.",
